1
00:00:09,084 --> 00:00:12,772
When did it start? Where did
it go? Is it the same one?

2
00:00:12,852 --> 00:00:15,222
Each question asks where a thing is.

3
00:00:16,024 --> 00:00:18,652
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:18,732 --> 00:00:22,610
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:26,374
Part 1 set two logics side by side.

6
00:00:26,454 --> 00:00:28,793
The logic of substance starts with things,

7
00:00:28,873 --> 00:00:30,532
and asks what happens to them.

8
00:00:30,612 --> 00:00:35,314
The logic of dependency asks how
anything is identified as a thing at all.

9
00:00:35,394 --> 00:00:39,173
And the famous refusals, neither
existent nor non existent,

10
00:00:39,253 --> 00:00:41,768
turned out to be a failed presupposition.

11
00:00:41,848 --> 00:00:44,178
No bearer, so neither answer.

12
00:00:44,976 --> 00:00:49,330
Here I turn the logic of dependency on
the questions we ask about anything.

13
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:54,652
Nāgārjuna opens his Middle Way by
paying homage to dependent arising,

14
00:00:54,732 --> 00:00:57,687
as free of eight extremes, in four pairs.

15
00:00:57,767 --> 00:00:59,358
Arising and ceasing.

16
00:00:59,438 --> 00:01:02,659
Permanence and annihilation.
Coming and going.

17
00:01:02,739 --> 00:01:04,580
Identity and difference.

18
00:01:05,384 --> 00:01:09,018
Under the logic of substance,
these are not extremes at all.

19
00:01:09,098 --> 00:01:13,325
They are simply the questions one asks
about anything. When did it start?

20
00:01:13,405 --> 00:01:16,871
When will it end? Does it
last, or is it destroyed?

21
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:19,466
Where did it come from,
and where did it go?

22
00:01:19,546 --> 00:01:21,848
Is it the same as that, or different?

23
00:01:22,644 --> 00:01:24,946
Every one of these assumes the same thing.

24
00:01:25,026 --> 00:01:26,998
That there is something with whereabouts.

25
00:01:27,078 --> 00:01:30,557
A position in time, in
space, or in identity,

26
00:01:30,637 --> 00:01:32,777
belonging to it from its own side.

27
00:01:33,592 --> 00:01:37,090
Arising and ceasing place it
at the two ends of a line.

28
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:40,813
Permanence keeps it on the line,
and annihilation removes it.

29
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:43,679
Coming and going move it
from one place to another.

30
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:47,746
Identity and difference set it beside
something else, to be compared.

31
00:01:48,548 --> 00:01:52,413
As I see it, the eight extremes
are not eight separate errors.

32
00:01:52,493 --> 00:01:55,297
They are eight ways of
asking where a thing is.

33
00:01:56,112 --> 00:02:00,357
The logic of dependency does not answer
these questions in a subtler way.

34
00:02:00,437 --> 00:02:03,210
It does not say the
thing arises invisibly,

35
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:07,055
lasts in a hidden form, or
goes somewhere we cannot see.

36
00:02:07,135 --> 00:02:10,574
It says that what was supposed
to have whereabouts is not found.

37
00:02:10,654 --> 00:02:13,147
And so the questions lose their object.

38
00:02:13,948 --> 00:02:15,394
When did it come into being?

39
00:02:15,474 --> 00:02:19,063
No thing is found crossing an
edge, from absent to present.

40
00:02:19,143 --> 00:02:22,369
It began at noon still
holds, as convention.

41
00:02:23,168 --> 00:02:25,022
What stays the same underneath?

42
00:02:25,102 --> 00:02:27,757
No carrier is found beneath the change.

43
00:02:28,572 --> 00:02:31,866
Where did it go? No
whereabouts are found after.

44
00:02:31,946 --> 00:02:33,949
The question does not apply.

45
00:02:34,744 --> 00:02:37,766
Is it the same as that, or
something else entirely?

46
00:02:37,846 --> 00:02:39,777
The sprout is not the seed.

47
00:02:39,857 --> 00:02:44,605
And yet rice yields rice. Not
identical. Not wholly other.

48
00:02:45,404 --> 00:02:50,831
Switch off a lamp. The room is dark, and
the light went nowhere. Switch it on.

49
00:02:50,911 --> 00:02:53,861
The room fills, and the
light came from nowhere.

50
00:02:53,941 --> 00:02:57,747
Both are true of every appearance,
and both were true all along.

51
00:02:57,827 --> 00:02:59,948
Nothing has been taken from the lamp.

52
00:03:00,028 --> 00:03:02,326
Only the question, where did the light go,

53
00:03:02,406 --> 00:03:04,178
has nothing left to be about.

54
00:03:04,992 --> 00:03:06,723
Now the decisive point.

55
00:03:06,803 --> 00:03:10,519
It is easy to miss, and for me
it is the heart of this part.

56
00:03:11,332 --> 00:03:15,536
Dependent arising is not one thing,
and the eight negations another.

57
00:03:15,616 --> 00:03:18,199
As if what arises in
dependence were then also,

58
00:03:18,279 --> 00:03:20,672
mysteriously, free of arising.

59
00:03:20,752 --> 00:03:24,087
The negations describe
dependent arising itself.

60
00:03:24,896 --> 00:03:27,832
If a sprout could be found
arising from its seed,

61
00:03:27,912 --> 00:03:29,861
it would have an arising of its own.

62
00:03:29,941 --> 00:03:31,954
And then it would not need to depend.

63
00:03:32,034 --> 00:03:36,519
That it depends is exactly why no
arising is found, when it is sought.

64
00:03:36,599 --> 00:03:39,657
Dependence and unfindability are one fact.

65
00:03:39,737 --> 00:03:43,697
Seen from the side of convention,
and from the side of analysis.

66
00:03:44,508 --> 00:03:49,201
So I do not hold emptiness in one hand,
and dependent arising in the other.

67
00:03:49,281 --> 00:03:50,755
It is one hand.

68
00:03:51,568 --> 00:03:56,574
Once the things are seen through, a new
temptation comes. Keep the relations.

69
00:03:56,654 --> 00:03:59,577
There are no things, but
everything is connected.

70
00:03:59,657 --> 00:04:01,374
The web is what is real.

71
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:05,216
But the relations are named
together with what they relate.

72
00:04:05,296 --> 00:04:09,699
A connection between two things that have
no standing of their own is not a third

73
00:04:09,779 --> 00:04:14,699
thing with standing. Looked for, the
web is not found on its own side either.

74
00:04:14,779 --> 00:04:17,539
The relating is as empty
as what it relates.

75
00:04:17,619 --> 00:04:19,663
And it works exactly as well.

76
00:04:20,472 --> 00:04:22,149
Now, identity.

77
00:04:23,044 --> 00:04:25,654
Under the logic of substance, what is it,

78
00:04:25,734 --> 00:04:29,042
and is it the same, have answers
hidden in the thing itself.

79
00:04:29,122 --> 00:04:33,281
A thing is what its essence makes it, and
it stays the same thing as long as the

80
00:04:33,361 --> 00:04:34,698
essence stays.

81
00:04:35,504 --> 00:04:38,173
The logic of dependency
moves the question.

82
00:04:38,253 --> 00:04:40,931
Identity is not what a thing is in itself.

83
00:04:41,011 --> 00:04:44,776
It is how the thing is reliably
picked out. Is it the same?

84
00:04:44,856 --> 00:04:50,229
becomes: the same by which criteria, for
which purpose, within which framework?

85
00:04:51,036 --> 00:04:55,566
A cracked phone is the same phone, for
the repair shop and for the insurer.

86
00:04:55,646 --> 00:05:00,009
A ship whose every plank has been
replaced is the same ship on the register,

87
00:05:00,089 --> 00:05:03,392
and perhaps not for the museum
that kept the old planks.

88
00:05:03,472 --> 00:05:07,074
The child in an old photograph
is you, for your family,

89
00:05:07,154 --> 00:05:11,739
your birth certificate, and the story
that runs from that afternoon to this one.

90
00:05:12,544 --> 00:05:15,186
Each answer is correct
within its framework.

91
00:05:15,266 --> 00:05:18,573
None is found in the thing,
apart from the framework.

92
00:05:19,388 --> 00:05:22,070
This does not make identity arbitrary.

93
00:05:22,150 --> 00:05:25,345
Criteria can be applied
rightly or wrongly.

94
00:05:25,425 --> 00:05:27,505
A forged passport fails.

95
00:05:27,585 --> 00:05:31,201
A mistaken face in a crowd
is corrected when it turns.

96
00:05:31,281 --> 00:05:35,522
What has gone is only the further claim,
that beneath the criteria there is a

97
00:05:35,602 --> 00:05:37,944
sameness from the thing's own side.

98
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:44,106
Identity seemed the most undeniable
thing there was. I am I. This is this.

99
00:05:44,186 --> 00:05:46,483
Seen this way, it is not less real.

100
00:05:46,563 --> 00:05:48,942
Its reality is of a different kind.

101
00:05:49,022 --> 00:05:51,800
The reality of a designation that works.

102
00:05:52,612 --> 00:05:55,363
The same shift changes
the word conventional.

103
00:05:56,168 --> 00:06:00,196
The logic of substance hears
it as a demotion. Agreed on.

104
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:01,812
Perhaps arbitrary.

105
00:06:01,892 --> 00:06:03,647
Certainly less than real.

106
00:06:03,727 --> 00:06:07,958
And so the path must lead from the
conventional to something truer behind it.

107
00:06:08,772 --> 00:06:13,257
For the logic of dependency, conventional
truth is the only kind of validity there

108
00:06:13,337 --> 00:06:16,876
is, and it is fully
valid. It has standards.

109
00:06:16,956 --> 00:06:18,628
Tsongkhapa gives three.

110
00:06:18,708 --> 00:06:20,925
What is known to ordinary cognition.

111
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:23,941
Not overturned by further
ordinary cognition.

112
00:06:24,021 --> 00:06:26,998
And not contradicted by
analysis of the ultimate.

113
00:06:27,078 --> 00:06:29,661
The snake in the rope
fails the second test.

114
00:06:29,741 --> 00:06:32,677
The inherently existing
rope fails the third.

115
00:06:32,757 --> 00:06:35,997
The rope, as named, passes all three.

116
00:06:36,808 --> 00:06:39,450
Convention is not the opposite of truth.

117
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:43,150
It is where truth, in
every usable sense, lives.

118
00:06:43,964 --> 00:06:48,060
And there is no second, deeper truth
for convention to fall short of.

119
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:50,478
The ultimate is not a higher world.

120
00:06:50,558 --> 00:06:52,407
It is the emptiness of this one.

121
00:06:52,487 --> 00:06:55,197
There is one appearance, seen two ways.

122
00:06:55,992 --> 00:06:59,309
Next time one of these questions
comes, notice its shape,

123
00:06:59,389 --> 00:07:01,039
before trying to answer it.

124
00:07:01,852 --> 00:07:04,987
Where did that feeling go?
Look for the place it went.

125
00:07:05,792 --> 00:07:07,849
Is this the same person I married?

126
00:07:07,929 --> 00:07:11,876
Ask, the same by which
criteria, for which purpose?

127
00:07:12,684 --> 00:07:14,307
Is this only conventional?

128
00:07:14,387 --> 00:07:18,007
Ask what you hoped would stand
behind it. And look for that.

129
00:07:18,808 --> 00:07:22,944
This is Section 4, Part 2 of
the Dependent Arising series.

130
00:07:23,756 --> 00:07:26,493
The question does not
need a cleverer answer.

131
00:07:26,573 --> 00:07:29,432
It needs to be seen, for what it assumes.

